# The image needs only docker/entrypoint.sh and the Lua scripts in
# docker/custom/ from this repository; everything else it contains is
# downloaded and verified during the build.
#
# So instead of listing what to leave out (.git, .env with its password,
# .runtime/, backups/, *.tar.gz, game data ...), ignore everything and allow
# just those back in. The build context stays a few kilobytes no matter
# what accumulates in the checkout - which also keeps `my-tes3mp deploy` fast,
# since it sends the context over SSH.
#
# (The Dockerfile itself is always sent, ignored or not.)
*
!docker/
docker/*
!docker/entrypoint.sh
!docker/custom/
!VERSION
